{"kind":"artifact","text":"Exact-head evidence for the MCP read surface, rebased onto main 0ba86570 and composing with the landed #6356 contracts. The work tool declares a fourth staleness policy, summary, which is now what a caller who names none gets: it returns the work still owed and reports what it left out in closed_stale_omitted, and its text summary says how to list those rows. The status and wait lanes stop reopening a satisfied or withdrawn commitment for ordinary staleness; ActorTotals counts it per status and splits artifact counts into retired and superseded-world. Composition with #6356: the only change to the work tool registration is its stale enum, which gains summary, and its description; the exact-path artifact query, the bounded limits and the authoritative fold ruling on writes are untouched. Every row the default still returns carries the full #6356 enrichment, including conditions, report_status, reported_head and latest_review with its non-omitted ratified, retired and stale flags, so a reader loses no review evidence, only closed history. Conditions met: (1) the default MCP status and work views summarize ordinary staleness while retired and superseded-world facts stay individually visible; (2) no information loss, since stale=include, only and exclude each return exactly what they returned before, every listed row still carries its own stale field, and full_projection_at names the detail routes; (4) TestExplicitStalePoliciesStillReturnEveryRecord and TestWorkQueryDefaultsIncludeAddressedWorkWithoutWaitingDebt pin both presentations, and mutating the default policy back to include turns them red. Tests passed: gofmt clean, go vet clean, go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, including go test ./cmd/gitseq-mcp.","body":{"branch":"request/staleness-presentation","commit":"d52dfbfa4b33321534ba2879ea3f170b971dc45b","head":"d52dfbfa4b33321534ba2879ea3f170b971dc45b","path":"cmd/gitseq-mcp"}}